{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1312348-do-klaives-need-to-be-activated","id":1312348,"title":"Do Klaives need to be activated?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-15T11:27:34-07:00","id":1312348,"title":"Do Klaives need to be activated?","content":"Rereading the W20 Klaive description I'm not sure if they actually need to be activated when combating other Garou, but I can see two possibilities:<br /> <br /> 1. The Klaive needs to be activated to get the +2 damage (although it would still do &quot;Strength&quot; aggravated damage since it is silver).<br /> 2. The Klaive only needs to be activated to inflict aggravated damage on non-shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T13:14:24-07:00","id":1312390,"title":"","content":"1) The +2 damage is just the weapon rating of the sword, so that doesn't need to get activated.<br /> 2) If there was meant to be an activation, this would probably be it.<br /> <br /> I think, largely informed by past WtA books, that you don't actually need to activate a &quot;base-line&quot; Klaive, but each one is supposed to be meticulously made and unique, and should have some activation bonus that's lesser than a Grand Klaive's activation ability. Consider that a Grand Klaive gets all the bonuses a normal one does and then you can activate it for something more, rather than needing to activate it to do it's base weapon damage or agg to anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T13:59:33-07:00","id":1312406,"title":"","content":"Klaives just need to be attuned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T01:28:17-07:00","id":1312506,"title":"","content":"To get basic Klaive abilities? No, they don't However without any Klaivaskar rules currently for 20th (although there are previous editions) they do feel a little lack-luster compared to other Fetishes and even some gifts. As a house rule 9while I am working up some Klaivaskar stuff anyway) I allow for Activation of a Klaive or Grandklaive to double it's base damage bonus. Of course Grandklaives get their other power too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T06:18:45-07:00","id":1312550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1312348-do-klaives-need-to-be-activated?p=1312406#post1312406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Klaives just need to be attuned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a page reference for that.<br /> <br /> I would think the agg damage to non-silver-weakness-victims is tied to being activated...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T07:16:06-07:00","id":1312562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1312348-do-klaives-need-to-be-activated?p=1312550#post1312550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a page reference for that.<br /> <br /> I would think the agg damage to non-silver-weakness-victims is tied to being activated...</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 221 as a general rule.<br /> Also in page 225 is mentioned that A war-spirit is usually bound into the klaive, allowing it to inflict aggravated damage even to non-Garou foes.<br /> According to that an activation roll allows the klaive to do aggravated to all foes, since all fetishes need to have their spirits roused with gnosis.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 05-16-2019, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T08:09:36-07:00","id":1312571,"title":"","content":"Thank you all very much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T15:54:20-07:00","id":1312663,"title":"","content":"While Activating is a General Rule the only part in the Klaives description that requires Activation is the secondary power of the Grand Klaive. Most of the fetish weapons in fact state if they have an activation requirement or not (for example, the Fang Dagger and the D'siah) but the base damage code and type is the default of the weapon. Klaivaskar for example in both it's previous forms could never actually be used with a Klaive if anything was otherwise and a D'siah apparently cuts for agg damage and the activation happens after that and that's before we get into things like cyberfetishes. Alternatively you can think of the attuning roll as the activation roll for things like Klaives with an power duration of &quot;Until new owner attunes&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T07:49:32-07:00","id":1312754,"title":"","content":"That's for Grand Klaive <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2767_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2767\" data-vbnamecard=\"2767\">Moirdryd</a> , not the Klaive. Which has a ''when the klaive is activated'' reference. Which mostly means that with the Gnosis roll the Grand Klaive does aggravated and activates a second power with one activation roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T10:57:19-07:00","id":1312974,"title":"","content":"What I am saying is that most of the weapons have their Stat-line always on and it is anything else they do that requires an activation. Case in point being the Fang dagger that does lethal damage unless it is activated in which case it doubles damage and that damage becomes agg, or the D'siah which has an activation for a specific effect that is done after damage and is the only power the weapon has, but it's stat line is an agg weapon. If you make the damage line of a Klaive require an activation roll then there is never any point in taking a Klaive, you'll be more dangerous without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T12:46:55-07:00","id":1313002,"title":"","content":"That's correct, the type of a weapon will always do its base damage without activation which is +2 for a Klaive and +5 for a Grand Klaive ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T15:56:45-07:00","id":1313205,"title":"","content":"+2A for a Klaive and +5A for a Grand Klaive, +2A for a D'siah, +1L for a Fang Dagger or +1A doubled if it's activated,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T10:19:16-07:00","id":1313331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1312348-do-klaives-need-to-be-activated?p=1313205#post1313205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+2A for a Klaive and +5A for a Grand Klaive, +2A for a D'siah, +1L for a Fang Dagger or +1A doubled if it's activated,</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a minute fang dagger doubles its damage modifier from +1 to +2, or all the damage you do after enemy soak like in revised ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T10:37:39-07:00","id":1313335,"title":"","content":"Doubles all successes on the damage roll Before soak and makes the damage Aggravated (thus often eliminating soak for lots of beasties) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T10:46:45-07:00","id":1313336,"title":"","content":"Correct ! Brokeeeen !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T10:56:42-07:00","id":1313339,"title":"","content":"But no Rage spending on that turn, which is why the Activate for damage weapons tend to be low Fetish rating and things like Klaives are high fetish rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T11:57:48-07:00","id":1313351,"title":"","content":"While not expressed this way in the books, as an emergent property? Fang Daggers are a Ragabash weapon. Use those stealthy powers to ambush people with a huge Agg damage attack, since you don't have the Rage to be the blender of doom of the Galliards and Ahrouns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T16:12:53-07:00","id":1313410,"title":"","content":"Yep, it's a common weapon for a Ragabash but then so is the Assassin Klaive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T03:40:52-07:00","id":1313463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1312348-do-klaives-need-to-be-activated?p=1313410#post1313410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, it's a common weapon for a Ragabash but then so is the Assassin Klaive</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that redundant? I mean, it is a fetish from a Shadow Lord TB, but its poweres are similar enough to Ragabash gifts/Rites of various editions, so a regular agg dealing weapon or mundane silver knife would surfice. Fearie Weapon from the Fianna TB is a fairly low cost fetish that does agg as its only power and is like a catch-all fetish for magical items of other supernaturals that a garou might get his hands on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T03:46:45-07:00","id":1313466,"title":"","content":"Yep, but it still happens. <br /> TBH Klaives (regular not Grand) are kind of annoying without Klaivaskar to back them up as any Rank 1 Theurge could get a silver weapon made and then perform a Rite of Awakening on it and have something that will be functional as a weapon and utterly deadly to most shifters. (Although that said I am working on an ST Vault project to do with stuff like this).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T18:55:48-07:00","id":1313602,"title":"","content":"Klaives do not need to be activated. Level four fetishes have a constant secondary power that need not to be activated, and Klaives happen to be one of them. Reference is Storyteller's Handbook (Revised)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/530270133407711244/580573002370908200/unknown.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T14:00:24-07:00","id":1313903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1312348-do-klaives-need-to-be-activated?p=1313602#post1313602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Klaives do not need to be activated. Level four fetishes have a constant secondary power that need not to be activated, and Klaives happen to be one of them. Reference is Storyteller's Handbook (Revised)</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm your reference is misunderstood, it doesn't say that, it only gives a rank 4 fetish general (and probably optional) rule, and the quote ''klaive dealing silver damage'' doesn't really help. Klaives do silver damage coz they are made of silver and their power to do aggravated to all targets is their major power, not a secondary one, Plus in W20 its a general rule for all fetishes their activation roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T14:09:09-07:00","id":1313904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1312348-do-klaives-need-to-be-activated?p=1313466#post1313466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, but it still happens.<br /> TBH Klaives (regular not Grand) are kind of annoying without Klaivaskar to back them up as any Rank 1 Theurge could get a silver weapon made and then perform a Rite of Awakening on it and have something that will be functional as a weapon and utterly deadly to most shifters. (Although that said I am working on an ST Vault project to do with stuff like this).</div> </div> </div> </div>Klaives are deadly because they are doing aggravated damage to all targets and you can use them with sword manouvers, parry, reposte, etc. Awakened silver blades might be more durable but they still won't do aggravated damage to non-shifters. Klaives might look weaker than they should, but they are stronger than meets the eye.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T15:40:30-07:00","id":1313918,"title":"","content":"You would think so until you realize that a ton of things also don't soak lethal. Klaives are stronger because of the lack of activation requirements otherwise if you need a weapon you just go Fang Dagger or you just go with Claws and Rage (and maybe Razor Claws because who doesn't want to hit as hard as a Klaive at diff 5?). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T06:50:17-07:00","id":1314053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1312348-do-klaives-need-to-be-activated?p=1313918#post1313918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would think so until you realize that a ton of things also don't soak lethal. Klaives are stronger because of the lack of activation requirements otherwise if you need a weapon you just go Fang Dagger or you just go with Claws and Rage (and maybe Razor Claws because who doesn't want to hit as hard as a Klaive at diff 5?).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now you scratch wounds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />!<br /> You know something, the truth is that is nowhere written that a klaive specifically needs to be activated to do aggravated damage, another example is the D'siah that always does aggravated damage to Wyrm creatures with no activation roll.<br /> <br /> Klaives would be awesome if the were unsoakable by normal armor or wyrm creatures, not just werewolves.<br /> <br /> Truth is that damage escalation in W20 is a bit confusing.<br /> <br /> For me Razor Claws do +1 damage at -1 difficulty, I deny to use the W20 version <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What are the stats for Labrys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 05-24-2019, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}